From cdf04b9d0b3e9015ffcce72fd48e59f359864856 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 01:06:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): scope the worker-subprocess tool fence to fenced
 boards, like the DB fence [daveey]

A Kanban worker's terminal/execute_code subprocesses carry HERMES_DELEGATED_CHILD_CONTEXT=<board root>.
The DB fence refuses writes only to the pinned board and boards under that root, but every kanban_*
tool refused once the marker was set, whatever board it targeted. A worker asked for a live
kanban_link / kanban_block refusal on a throwaway board had no route and handed an ssh command back
to the user (defect agent-cbb2687c75, t_01a194ea280f2a75).

- _reject_delegated_child_mutation(tool, args): for board-local writes (worker-guarded lifecycle tools,
  link/unlink, comment, explicitly local create) an env-fenced subprocess is refused only when the
  target board or HERMES_HOME lies inside the fence (kanban_path_is_fenced). In-process delegate
  children, the legacy '1' marker and an unresolvable path stay refused everywhere; archive, origin
  adoption, supervisor requests and non-local creates (may write another gateway) always refuse.
- The fence refusal texts (DB and tool) name the scratch-home route: mktemp -d ~/kanban-probe.XXXX,
  unset the board pins, rm -rf afterwards.
- tests/tools/test_kanban_tools_scratch_home_fence.py: scratch home reaches the real unknown-parent
  refusal (in-process and a real owner-bound subprocess); board under the root, pinned DB, fenced
  home, legacy marker and in-process delegate child stay refused.

- The fence helpers move to tools/kanban_tools_fence.py (re-exported from kanban_tools) to keep that file under its line cap.
